# promise: #613
# ⌘S as Arc does it (the reporter's 120 fps side-by-side, measured frame by frame): the page is resized to its card
# every frame of the sidebar's slide and reflows as the edge moves, instead of being sized for where it ends up and
# jumping when the slide ends. The page's edge beside the sidebar travels with the card; the far edge stays put, so
# the right side doesn't jump (#317's point).
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
pace 0.5
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=slide
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://action/toggleSidebar
expect-log sidebar slide: page moved [0-9]+ pt over [0-9]+ frames \(near edge ([3-9][0-9]|[1-9][0-9]{2,}) pt, far edge [01] pt, live\)
cra://action/toggleSidebar
wait 0.5
reject-log sidebar slide: .*far edge ([2-9]|[1-9][0-9]+) pt
# Docking the sidebar from over the page (#483's path) resizes the page as it goes too, its far edge still put.
cra://action/toggleSidebar
wait 1
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=1
wait 1
cra://debug?windowState=out
expect-log window state out: main0 .* sidebar=left edge=floating
cra://action/toggleSidebar
wait 1
expect-log sidebar docked in place: page moved ([3-9][0-9]|[1-9][0-9]{2,}) pt$
reject-log sidebar slide: .*far edge ([2-9]|[1-9][0-9]+) pt
